{
  "dom_id": "step-q3529",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Factor $27{c}^{3}+1.$",
  "worked_solution": "The sum of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}+{b}^{3}=(a+b)({a}^{2}-ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a sum of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n27{c}^{3}+1=(3c)^{3}+{1}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the sum of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27{c}^{3}+1 & =(3c)^{3}+{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(3c+1)((3c)^{2}-3c\\cdot 1+{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(3c+1)(9{c}^{2}-3c+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
